  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Framework Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now diving into the framework guidelines, specifically the full-stack setup instructions. The instruction regarding server entry points and Express setup, plus the vital `vite.middlewares` integration are top of mind. I\'m keen on how this affects my configuration and if it provides better options than my prior plans. I\'m also scoping for more on this \"start\" process.\n\n\n**Verifying Dev Script Strategy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `package.json`\'s dev script, specifically how it handles a full-stack backend with `server.ts`. Currently, the suggested setup uses `tsx server.ts` when a backend is present. I\'m checking how Vite\'s middleware interacts with Express in development, confirming the Vite server creation and `vite.middlewares` integration within `server.ts`. I want to verify if the standard pattern applies to AI studio and see how the configuration aligns.\n\n\n**Analyzing Metadata Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the server with the metadata and HTML. I\'m focusing on syncing the metadata in `metadata.json` such as name and description, with the title and meta descriptions within `index.html`. My first turn requirements must set the correct values and never rename them. Permissions and capabilities are maintained, including the `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API`. I\'m going to replace placeholder values on this first turn.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Analytical Nodes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on orchestrating five distinct analytical nodes for this market intelligence engine. I\'m thinking about how to route and process information non-linearly, avoiding simple search and summarization. The key challenge is to manage the flow of data through these isolated environments, incorporating adversarial stress-testing and epistemic certainty checks. I\'m prioritizing non-linear ingestion and processing to meet the engine\'s architectural needs.\n\n\n**Enforcing Architecture Protocols**\n\nI\'m now implementing emergency architectural protocols to enhance the engine. The zero data leakage law is critical, demanding the `source_url` metadata attribute always accompany each empirical metric. I\'m focusing on the contradiction isolation directive, which forces debate during collisions. Also, I\'m ensuring schema guardrails for data communication across nodes. I am now working on Phase 1, Dynamic Persona Synthesizer.\n\n\n**Implementing Persona Instruction**\n\nI\'m now expanding each qualitative persona instruction into a branching tree. This tree will have three root tracks, each mapped to two advanced, multi-parameter web search strings. I\'m ensuring explicit geo-anchors, operational terminology, and industry descriptors are included. I\'m also planning nested leaf queries for any volatile or missing text to fill in the gaps. The output will follow a strict JSON layout, as per the specifications.\n\n\n**Defining Delphi Panel Phases**\n\nI\'m now outlining Phase 4, the Multi-Perspective Delphi Panel Consensus, and Phase 5, the Bi-Directional Adversarial Debate. I need to concurrently initialize the three expert personas from Phase 1, followed by generating independent briefs and identifying blind spots. Phase 5 will then include a two-round debate between expansion (optimist) and risk auditor (pessimist) agents to resolve contradictions, adhering to the forced debate mandate. I\'ll focus on how `conflict_details` will be integrated.\n\n\n**Compiling Final Report**\n\nI\'m now implementing Phase 6: the Master Investment Report Compiler. I\'m focusing on assembling a fully hyperlinked Markdown report with an executive summary that will be highly objective. The tone is clinical and authoritative, with seven structural sections. The primary data source will be the adjudicated claims which will contain the verdict justification, Epistemic Certainty and Risk Status.\n\n\n**Structuring Report Outputs**\n\nI\'m now detailing the final report\'s structure, focusing on the core deliverables for the user. I need to make a **GO/NO-GO INVESTMENT DECISION**, with supporting elements. The report components will include: Dynamic Delphi Expert Briefs with a Markdown table of operational variables, an Adversarial Stress-Test Audit Report (BAC LOG), a Systematic Certainty & Risk Matrix, a Strategic Roadmap with De-risking Blueprint, and a Verified Reference Index with source citations. I\'m focusing on user presentation and clarity.\n\n\n**Visualizing Node Execution**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the live orchestration stream. I want to build a real-time visualization of each node\'s execution using Server-Sent Events (SSE). It must show animated statuses, telemetry, logs, and raw data payloads with interactive JSON inspectability. I\'m prioritizing the visualization of the Dynamic Persona Synthesizer, Tree-of-Thought Router, MapReduce Ingestion Grid, and Delphi Panel Consensus.\n\n\n**Refining Node 6 Output**\n\nI\'m currently focused on Node 6, the Master Investment Report Compiler, and its output. I\'m prioritizing features like a two-round live adversarial transcript, a judge\'s verdict, and Epistemic Certainty gauge cards. I\'ll also add rendered Markdown with footnotes, and JSON export for the entire pipeline state. My goals include flexible filters and robust error handling to use Gemini API and ensure real-time data integrity. I\'m working on allowing users to pause, inspect, and re-run.\n\n\n**Designing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the UI aesthetic for the final investment report and overall studio experience. I\'m aiming for a Bloomberg/Palantir-inspired dark mode palette with specific color codes to indicate status: GO/verified (emerald), disputed (amber), and unhedged risks (crimson). Also, I\'m evaluating the package dependencies needed for the frontend, considering `canvas-confetti` for decision celebrations, and markdown rendering options. A custom markdown renderer seems preferable.\n\n\n**Validating API Endpoints**\n\nNow I\'m designing API endpoints within `server.ts` to execute the pipeline stages, and stream their progress via Server-Sent Events (SSE). I\'m focusing on modularizing the `/api/pipeline` endpoints for a granular control. I want `/api/pipeline/run` for an end-to-end orchestrated run. Then I am considering individual endpoints (`/api/pipeline/phase1-dps` ...) to stream step-by-step progress using `text/event-stream`. I\'m going to make sure the Gemini API is initialized and streaming is working well.\n\n\n**Configuring Gemini Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Google GenAI `gemini-3.8-flash` model, focusing on the `server.ts` setup. I\'ve configured the API key and User-Agent headers and am verifying the model\'s capabilities. I\'m carefully considering how to handle search grounding, either with the `googleSearch` tool or `responseMimeType: \"application/json\"`. The API\'s restrictions around combining these features are a key point to investigate.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 697296386
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "pb-8aqfaMtKFxN8P7KXzsQs"
  }
}
