    thinking: "**Planning Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on constructing the frontend elements. My plan starts with `src/components/Header.tsx`, including the title \"Researchify AI,\" the subtitle \"Autonomous Multi-Perspective Market Intelligence & Adversarial Verification Engine,\" and a live system status indicator. I\'m prioritizing the header as the initial component to establish a clear visual foundation.\n\n\n**Designing Action Controls**\n\nMy current focus is on the action controls within the frontend. I\'m designing functionality for new inquiries, a presets drawer, exporting audit dossiers in JSON or Markdown, and a history modal. I want to build a set of intuitive controls to facilitate comprehensive user interaction with the system.\n\n\n**Visualizing Deep Phase**\n\nI\'m now diving into the deep phase visualizer components. I\'m building out components for each phase: Phase1 displays expert dossiers and mandates; Phase2 visualizes expert branches as interactive tree nodes; Phase3 features mapper workers and a reducer collision radar; and Phase4 presents tabbed expert briefs with infrastructure and risk analysis.\n\n\n**Constructing Adversarial Views**\n\nI\'m now implementing the adversarial debate transcript in `Phase5AdversarialView.tsx`. This includes the structure for Round 1 collisions and Round 2 rebuttals between optimistic and pessimistic experts. I\'m also adding epistemic certainty gauges and adjudicated claim cards to assess risk and inform decision posture badges. Lastly, I\'m constructing the formatted executive market intelligence reports and adding raw json inspectors for deep validation. Real-time terminal log streams will be added in the final phases.\n\n\n"
