  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Error Source**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core of the problem: a 429 error, indicating a quota exceedance during Phase 3\'s search grounding. This points directly to the API\'s rate limits. I am checking the user\'s plan and billing details now to confirm and ensure they\'re appropriately configured. I\'m also examining the specified error documentation.\n\n\n**Investigating Rate Limit Impact**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the implications of the rate limits. The documentation link provides insight into current usage. I am reviewing the `runPhase3MapReduce` code, specifically the rapid succession of calls using `googleSearch`, and considering if the user\'s quota tier is being exceeded, triggering those 429 errors during that phase\'s grounding search.\n\n\n**Implementing Rate Limit Solutions**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial issue: the `runPhase3MapReduce` function. The 429 errors from the search call led directly into a subsequent call to `ai.models.generateContent` for `reducerPrompt`, exacerbating the problem when quota\'s exhausted. I\'m focusing on implementing robust retry logic with exponential backoff and jitter for the Gemini API, specifically managing 429 errors. I\'m also planning to incorporate a fallback to a non-grounded empirical model extraction query when the Google Search tool encounters a 429.\n\n\n"
