  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Gemini Call Structure**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the `callGeminiSafe` function. I\'ve identified the need for primary and fallback model constants: \'gemini-3.8-flash\' and \'gemini-2.5-flash\', respectively. Also included is a simple `sleep` helper function, critical for managing API request rate limits.\n\n\n**Refining Gemini Call Function**\n\nI\'m now integrating the retry logic within `callGeminiSafe`. I\'ve set a `maxRetries` parameter with a default of 2. It will alternate between search and no-search requests. The configuration includes tool settings for the Google Search and the model parameter. The existing logic successfully extracts and formats search sources from responses.\n\n\n**Handling Error Conditions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on robust error handling within the call function, especially concerning rate limits and quotas. I\'ve implemented logic to identify 429 errors or quota issues and adjust the request accordingly. Specifically, if the search tool hits a quota, I will immediately retry without it. I\'m also implementing automatic model switching to the fallback model if a primary model hits a rate limit and a retry occurs.\n\n\n**Implementing Retry Logic**\n\nI\'ve added retry logic with exponential backoff to `callGeminiSafe`. If an attempt fails, it waits before retrying, handling various errors. I\'ve focused on graceful degradation, ensuring the process doesn\'t fail immediately. The function now handles rate limits and other failures. Also, I\'ve incorporated the retry mechanism within each phase that utilizes the function.\n\n\n**Analyzing Phase 3 Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the MapReduce phase, focusing on its data flow. I\'ve structured the search-grounding request in Phase 3. It utilizes the `callGeminiSafe` function to gather market research data, incorporating precise metrics and dates. The retry configuration is now set to a single attempt. I\'ve also incorporated error handling.\n\n\n**Adding API Request Spacing**\n\nI\'ve added a sleep function call within the stream endpoint to space out requests. Specifically, a 400ms delay now exists between each phase, preventing rapid API call bursts. I\'ve also incorporated SSE events to relay informational or warning logs in real time to the user during pipeline stages. Next, I\'m defining query-specific fallbacks using `generateContextualFacts`. For example, aviation/AAM prompts will trigger FAA part 135 topics.\n\n\n"
