  planner_response {
    response: "### Error Analysis & Fix Applied\n\n**Cause of the Error:**\nIn `src/components/NodePipelineTracker.tsx`, the outer navigation card for each phase was implemented as a `<button>` element. When a phase became eligible for step-by-step execution, an inner step trigger `<button>` (\"Run\") was rendered inside the outer button. According to the HTML5 specification and React DOM reconciliation, `<button>` cannot be a descendant of another `<button>`, resulting in the reported DOM validation and hydration warnings.\n\n---\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **`src/components/NodePipelineTracker.tsx`**:\n  - Replaced the outer interactive wrapper with an accessible `<div role=\"button\" tabIndex={0}>` complete with `onKeyDown` (Enter / Spacebar support) and focus rings.\n  - Preserved the inner step-by-step \"Run\" `<button>` with its isolated click propagation.\n  - Verified that all other interactive components throughout the application adhere to proper HTML element nesting."
    modified_response: "### Error Analysis & Fix Applied\n\n**Cause of the Error:**\nIn `src/components/NodePipelineTracker.tsx`, the outer navigation card for each phase was implemented as a `<button>` element. When a phase became eligible for step-by-step execution, an inner step trigger `<button>` (\"Run\") was rendered inside the outer button. According to the HTML5 specification and React DOM reconciliation, `<button>` cannot be a descendant of another `<button>`, resulting in the reported DOM validation and hydration warnings.\n\n---\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **`src/components/NodePipelineTracker.tsx`**:\n  - Replaced the outer interactive wrapper with an accessible `<div role=\"button\" tabIndex={0}>` complete with `onKeyDown` (Enter / Spacebar support) and focus rings.\n  - Preserved the inner step-by-step \"Run\" `<button>` with its isolated click propagation.\n  - Verified that all other interactive components throughout the application adhere to proper HTML element nesting."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
