    thinking: "**Examining German Pharma Regs**\n\nI\'ve been diving into German pharmaceutical regulations. I\'ve focused on the BfArM website and the Federal Ministry of Health\'s GMP guidelines. GenerisOnline has also proven to be a useful overview. My next step is fetching and analyzing the regulatory documents directly. I am verifying their live and official nature.\n\n\n**Refining Search Strategies**\n\nI\'m now experimenting with fetching web pages based on the user\'s query and the primary queries generated from the Tree-of-Thought during Phase 2. The idea is to execute these queries in parallel and aggregate real-time web results, including titles, URLs, and text snippets. I\'m also planning to incorporate Wikipedia API results to include verified academic and institutional sources and links, enriching the data with verified references.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Integrity Measures**\n\nI\'m now focused on integrating a robust zero-hallucination mechanism for data processing. This involves feeding a live web dataset directly into Gemini\'s MapReduce engine, enforcing strict rules against fabricated data or URLs. The goal is to ensure that every output is verifiable, linking directly to its source with live, clickable URLs. I am also implementing a \"Web Intel Stream\" badge in the UI to display the live scraping status.\n\n\n"
