    thinking: "**Examining Source Data**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the `Phase6ReportView.tsx` file, specifically the `report.sources` object. It looks like each source has an `id`, `title`, `url`, `claim_reference`, `publisher`, `date`, and `is_live_web` attribute. This is interesting considering the user\'s feedback that these sources may be fabricated. I am examining their report to discern what kind of information is missing, or contradictory.\n\n\n**Analyzing Source Reliability**\n\nI\'ve uncovered a potential vulnerability in the source data generation. It seems the system can fall back to constructing \"facts\" if Google News doesn\'t return enough results. This results in duplicate, or missing information. Furthermore, I need to evaluate if Gemini\'s responses were grounded in real web content. This fallback mechanism could explain the user\'s perception of fabricated sources.\n\n\n**Developing Research Engine**\n\nI\'m now focused on constructing a robust internet research engine within `server.ts`. I realize Gemini sometimes fabricates claims, especially without strict constraints. I\'ve also found Google News RSS links can fail to resolve without cookies, so I\'m implementing DuckDuckGo\'s organic web search. This will allow for direct URL extraction, real webpage titles, live snippet text, and publisher identification. This should solve the hallucination issue.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Integration**\n\nI\'m integrating several new data sources to enhance the research engine\'s reliability. I\'m leveraging the Wikipedia Knowledge API to gather technical and institutional definitions with real links. I\'m also including CrossRef to search for academic and regulatory DOIs, ensuring access to peer-reviewed studies and publications. This is in preparation for Phase 3: the Real Source Ingestion Grid.\n\n\n**Refining Fact Verification**\n\nI\'m now designing Phase 5, which features a debate between \"Optimist\" and \"Cynical Auditor\" personas, grounded in real source evidence, to validate any contradictory facts. Then, in Phase 6, the final report will directly link to each real article via footnotes and a \"Visit Real Web Source\" button. My focus is on absolute transparency, ensuring all information derives from and links to real, verifiable web documents.\n\n\n"
