    thinking: "**Observing Publisher Domains**\n\nI\'ve been looking over Google News RSS articles and have picked up on a key detail. The `<source url=\"...\">` tag consistently reveals the publisher\'s direct domain. For example, I\'ve observed this pattern with domains like `jobyaviation.com`, `smartcitiesdive.com`, and several others. It\'s a nice consistent pattern to make use of.\n\n\n**Expanding Query Capabilities**\n\nI\'ve realized I can enhance the data harvesting with a multi-pronged approach.  By using the Tree-of-Thought primary queries (regulatory, techno-economics, and failure modes), I can query OpenAlex, Wikipedia, Google News, and HackerNews for *each* track. This should yield a richer, more diverse set of results. I\'m excited about the potential for getting more relevant and nuanced data.\n\n\n**Defining Data Fields**\n\nI\'m solidifying the data model. I\'ve got key fields now: URL, publisher, date, snippet, and source type. I\'m focusing on ensuring these are accurate, valid, and consistently populated. The ingestion grid will feed Gemini 3.8 Flash, but its responses will be post-processed to verify sources. Gemini\'s output will have strict directives to cite verified URLs, and the post-processor will ensure source integrity.\n\n\n"
