  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Expanding Web Intel Gathering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on expanding the `fetchRealWebIntel` function. I\'ve realized its current sources are limited, only covering Google News, Wikipedia, and CrossRef. I\'ve analyzed Google News links, and noted a missing integration for OpenAlex, which I need to prioritize, as it\'s returning actual academic papers from publishers such as Nature, IEEE, and Elsevier.\n\n\n**Refining Intel Source Integration**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the sources. I\'ve integrated Hacker News Algolia, which provides direct links to tech and market articles. I\'ve also improved Wikipedia\'s query handling; I\'m no longer limiting it to just four keywords. CrossRef integration has been expanded, addressing the placeholder and row limitations. I\'ve also found problems with missing data to the LLM and the fallback claim generation!\n\n\n**Validating Empirical Data Points**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data validation. The recent Google News integration was producing results that seemed synthetic, not grounded in verifiable facts. My focus is on the `fetchRealWebIntel` function to ensure it\'s harvesting genuine, factual data. I\'m prioritizing direct extraction of empirical facts from each source, and working to implement precise citation of the URLs and publishers, and filtering based on publication date!\n\n\n**Enhancing Source Transparency**\n\nI\'m now integrating source details directly. I\'ve ensured the system now attaches real `source_snippets` to each record, enabling direct access to the source text. If Gemini encounters issues, the deterministic fallback generates factual records from the title, snippet, and date of each harvested item. These records contrast real sources, and I\'m ensuring every fact includes the article title, publisher, and link. I\'m also adding a \"Live Internet Intelligence Repository\" panel displaying this data, and I\'m updating the Fact cards to show publisher, title, snippet, and a \"Read Original Web Source\" button, and full details.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 977279715
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "hMe8atjpDNeR_uMPxqPPyQQ"
  }
