  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Source Population**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `sourcesMap` is populated within `runPhase6Report`. It seems it can draw source data from `mapReduce.raw_harvested_sources` or `r.source_snippets`. I\'m now examining the logic: if `r.source_snippets?.[uIdx]` exists, it\'s assigned to `ReportSource.snippet`. The process appears to have some interesting conditional behavior.\n\n\n**Analyzing Source Acquisition**\n\nI\'ve determined that if `verifiedSourcesList` is empty, the system populates from `raw_harvested_sources`. I\'m also planning the update to `server.ts`, focusing on lines 160-320. Within `fetchRealWebIntel`, I\'m looking at subquery generation, crafting targeted search queries: the primary query, and three others targeting research and economic/failure data. OpenAlex will be queried in parallel.\n\n\n**Enumerating Real Web Resources**\n\nI\'m now integrating external real-world data sources. I\'m extracting published papers, Wikipedia articles, HackerNews stories, Google News dispatches, and peer-reviewed papers using APIs. These are processed concurrently with timeouts and deduplication, aiming for a final data set of 15-30 real internet documents. I\'m moving on to `runPhase3MapReduce` next, examining how `realWebItems` is handled.\n\n\n**Integrating Real Web Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `realWebItems` gets integrated with `mapReduceOutput.raw_harvested_sources`. I\'m formatting the real web data to include source ID, title, publisher, URL, date, snippet, and source type. Then, I\'m examining the prompt\'s instructions to Gemini, emphasizing the use of *only* real internet records. I\'m also looking at the verification process for Gemini\'s responses, particularly the checks on `associated_sources` for valid URLs and the population of publishers, titles, and snippets from harvested records.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 438851621
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "nMe8asWmFvDF_PUPndPm8AE"
